WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.040
The "Jackass" crew have been called "the elder&nbsp;
statesmen of self-inflicted harm" — but time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.200
catches up with all of us. So now that Johnny&nbsp;
Knoxville and company have reached middle age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.960
is a fifth "Jackass" movie even&nbsp;
physically possible for them?
 &nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.120
Back in the '90s, Johnny Knoxville wasn't yet the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.320
star we know today. Much like one of his&nbsp;
influences, writer Hunter S. Thompson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.000
Knoxville was up for anything and everything,&nbsp;
including testing self-defense equipment on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.040
himself for "Big Brother" magazine.&nbsp;
His risk-taking didn't go unnoticed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.320
and before long the magazine was gaining&nbsp;
attention from other like-minded daredevils,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.680
including Steve-O. Soon enough, the likes of Chris&nbsp;
Pontius and Jason "Wee Man" Acuña came on board,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.800
bolstered by behind-the-scenes staff such as&nbsp;
Jeff Tremaine and Spike Jonze. This ragtag team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.760
made quirky videos for the early internet, and it&nbsp;
didn't take too long before people took notice.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.480
With the prospect of branching out into&nbsp;
a television show, a few more talents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.360
were added to the ranks, including skater Bam&nbsp;
Margera and his buddy, Ryan Dunn. This proved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.520
to be the final ingredient and, following some&nbsp;
network shopping, the crew signed up with MTV.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:07.120
"Jackass" made its television debut in April&nbsp;
2000 and was a near-overnight success. In no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.440
time at all, Knoxville went from doing random&nbsp;
commercials to make ends meet, to posing for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.680
the cover of Rolling Stone. The show's success&nbsp;
saw them break out onto the big screen in 2002,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:23.000
with "Jackass: The Movie." Three more movies would&nbsp;
follow, including 2022's "Jackass Forever."  
 &nbsp;

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.480
Following the box office success of 2010's&nbsp;
"Jackass 3D," the franchise was fairly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.040
dormant for most of the 2010s. The idea of&nbsp;
a fourth film never quite went away though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:38.000
with many fans still craving more. Sadly, in 2011,&nbsp;
cast member Ryan Dunn was killed in a car crash at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.120
the age of 34. This was a tremendous loss for&nbsp;
the crew, and his death was especially hard on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.134
Bam Margera, who had already been struggling with&nbsp;
substance abuse issues prior to Dunn's passing.

00:01:48.134 --> 00:01:54.671
"This is not right. It's not right."

00:01:54.671 --> 00:01:59.240
Margera's substance issues returned during the&nbsp;
production of "Jackass Forever," as Paramount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.920
Pictures was hesitant to allow him to appear in&nbsp;
the film. These fears were later substantiated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.240
when they became a source of conflict&nbsp;
between Margera and the film's producers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.640
including Jeff Tremaine, Spike Jonze, and Johnny&nbsp;
Knoxville. Margera even went as far as to publicly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:18.520
rant about his treatment on Instagram, alleging&nbsp;
he was being treated like an animal by the studio.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:23.080
He also threatened his former friends, resulting&nbsp;
in Tremaine slapping Margera with a restraining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.120
order. This resulted in Margera being fired&nbsp;
from "Jackass Forever" and, aside from one stunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:33.120
and a handful of background appearances,&nbsp;
he was removed from the film entirely.
 &nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.440
Aside from the very public break-up with Bam&nbsp;
Margera, another issue the "Jackass Forever"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.800
crew had to overcome was the COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;
which had put Hollywood on an indefinite pause.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.320
While most productions simply pumped the&nbsp;
brakes until they were allowed to resume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.440
the "Jackass" crew were given some leeway&nbsp;
by Paramount. The studio used the film as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.680
an excuse to see what future productions&nbsp;
could achieve during the pandemic. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.720
was confirmed by Wee Man during an interview&nbsp;
on "The Nine Club With Chris Roberts," where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.960
he also explained other ways the pandemic&nbsp;
affected production. It seems that the team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.040
wanted to film stuff on location in some exotic&nbsp;
locales. However, due to travel restrictions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.560
and the varying nature of COVID-19 testing in&nbsp;
different countries, this had to be scrapped.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.720
With the arrival of various vaccines, things&nbsp;
regarding COVID-19 have become much more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.320
manageable than they were at the pandemic's peak.&nbsp;
So with that hurdle removed, it'll likely be much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:26.280
easier to film a potential fifth theatrical&nbsp;
film, should they decide to pursue it.
 &nbsp;

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.120
"Jackass Forever" really did feel like&nbsp;
a changing of the guard for the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.440
especially when it came to the cast. While most&nbsp;
of the original cast was back for another round,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.920
this entry also introduced some new blood —&nbsp;
predominantly because many of the original crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:44.160
couldn't push themselves as hard as they used to.&nbsp;
The new cast featured Sean "Poopies" McInerney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:49.800
Zach Holmes, Jasper Dolphin, Eric Manaka, and&nbsp;
Rachel Wolfson. This means that "Jackass Forever"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.280
saw not only its first Black cast members&nbsp;
but its first female cast member as well.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.560
Change is never easy for any long-running&nbsp;
franchise but in this instance, the new additions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.640
didn't feel forced or reductive in any way. None&nbsp;
of them felt out of place and it even allowed for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:08.480
some fresh reactions to things that perhaps the&nbsp;
old cast might've been desensitized to. "Jackass"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.520
has always been a series built off of youthful&nbsp;
vigor, so this development makes absolute sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.680
and could see the franchise continuing even&nbsp;
when the OGs are no longer part of the crew.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:22.880
When it comes to the cast of "Jackass," you'd be&nbsp;
hard-pressed to find a member more dedicated than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.680
Steve-O. From swimming with sharks to bungee&nbsp;
jumping in an excrement-loaded porta potty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.534
Steve-O is the "Jackass" crew's indispensable man.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:34.520
However, that doesn't mean it's always been&nbsp;
peaches and cream for Steve-O. Both the third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:38.800
and fourth films were especially hard for the&nbsp;
self-proclaimed Wild Boy for different reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.320
"Jackass 3D" was Steve-O's first production&nbsp;
after achieving his sobriety — something the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:48.560
crew all helped him with. Despite his lifestyle&nbsp;
transition, Steve-O was still as gung ho as ever.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:53.000
When it came to "Jackass Forever" though, Steve-O&nbsp;
said in an interview with Entertainment Weekly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.840
that it was "kind of a bummer." He went on&nbsp;
to explain that this attitude stemmed from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.360
seeing what Johnny Knoxville was still&nbsp;
subjecting himself to physically at his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.160
age. He specifically referred to a stunt that&nbsp;
involved Knoxville being charged into by a bull,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.600
which resulted in severe brain&nbsp;
damage. Steve-O told the outlet:

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.311
"It's not fun to watch Knoxville&nbsp;
get hit in the head anymore."

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.400
"So what happened after it hit me?"

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.400
"Dude, it's gnarly."

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.280
As a result, it seems unlikely we'll&nbsp;
see Steve-O — or possibly any member of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:23.000
the "Jackass" crew — in a fifth feature film.&nbsp;
However, we may see them join forces for some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:27.960
other project. Speaking with CinemaBlend&nbsp;
in August 2023, the daredevil explained,

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.320
"I wouldn't be surprised if some&nbsp;
kind of project reunited us again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:34.120
but I wouldn't bet on there being another movie."

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.240
The "Jackass" movies have always been a bit of&nbsp;
an anomaly, as you wouldn't expect films of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:42.760
caliber to amass positive buzz from the press.&nbsp;
However, with the exception of the first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:47.400
all of the main theatrical films have positive&nbsp;
Rotten Tomatoes scores. "Jackass Forever" stands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:51.760
as the highest-rated entry in the entire&nbsp;
series and it isn't hard to see why. Nick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.280
Schager of Esquire described the original&nbsp;
cast as "elder statesman of self-inflicted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:00.080
harm" — which is an apt description if&nbsp;
we've ever heard one. Schager also wrote:

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.680
"In a pandemic era of extreme caution and fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:07.080
it's a welcome relief to watch Knoxville and the&nbsp;
rest risk life and limb for the sheer hell of it."

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:11.640
Many critics seemed to share the same sentiment,&nbsp;
with Brett Doze of InSession Film saying,

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.760
"I'm not going to pretend there is some&nbsp;
thought-provoking, underlying message&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:19.000
that wasn't there before, but I certainly did&nbsp;
enjoy laughing my ass off with these friends."

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.640
That ultimately might just be the appeal of&nbsp;
these movies — the feeling of reconnecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.966
with something or someone from your past.

00:06:24.966 --> 00:06:27.469
With "Jackass Forever" being both a critical 

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.960
and commercial success, many have wondered&nbsp;
if "Jackass 5" will be happening. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:36.360
as of September 2023, very little&nbsp;
has been said about a fifth film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.080
aside from a few scant comments. The&nbsp;
"Jackass" films aren't like other movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.200
as they don't have a screenplay or even a&nbsp;
three-act narrative. As opposed to a plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:49.067
the movies are more of an eclectic compilation&nbsp;
of crazy stunts and pranks of varying scales.

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:50.587
"My god."

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:51.720
"Are you crying?"

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:52.884
"I think he's hurt."

00:06:52.884 --> 00:06:56.400
Additionally, many of the best moments&nbsp;
in the films aren't even planned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.720
with several highlights originating as something&nbsp;
thought up on the spot. An example of this would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:05.520
be the "Rocky" prank from "Jackass 3D," wherein&nbsp;
Bam Margera would surprise someone with a splash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:10.480
of water and a punch to the head. You can't script&nbsp;
or coordinate spontaneity like that, and this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.920
a key factor in the films. If a fifth "Jackass"&nbsp;
movie was announced, we probably wouldn't see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:19.560
scrap of footage from it for a very long time.&nbsp;
However, when and if that day finally comes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:24.240
you can rest assured that hardcore fans of&nbsp;
the series will be waiting with bated breath.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.160
Much of the "Jackass" franchise's DNA&nbsp;
stems from Johnny Knoxville. From its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:32.520
humble origins to what it has become, the&nbsp;
man is undoubtedly the series' figurehead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.840
Though it might be a head that has been&nbsp;
rattled by a few sizable concussions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:38.480
it's still one that has helped&nbsp;
steer the ship since the beginning.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.400
Any mentions of a potential&nbsp;
fifth entry have been limited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.440
with Knoxville himself providing&nbsp;
the closest thing to an update.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:48.400
In an interview with Variety, Knoxville&nbsp;
addressed the future of the series, saying,

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:52.600
"We never said whether it was or wasn't [the final&nbsp;
film]. [...] If we did continue, we would lean on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:56.840
the younger cast more and the old guys would take&nbsp;
a little step back but still be a part of it."

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:59.360
"There may be another Jackass, there may not be."

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:03.240
Addressing his own part in a possible&nbsp;
"Jackass 5," Knoxville went on to add,

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.280
"I would have to step back because my neurologist&nbsp;
said I can't have any more concussions."

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:11.040
Knoxville is the lynchpin of the show, and&nbsp;
even if he did have to step back from some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.400
of the more physically demanding stunts, it still&nbsp;
would be great to see him play a part. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.567
"Jackass" wouldn't be the same without&nbsp;
Knoxville's infectious cackling.

00:08:18.567 --> 00:08:20.765
"Right?! God help me, I love it."

00:08:20.765 --> 00:08:22.560
Throughout the "Jackass" series and movies, 

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.040
we've seen different stunts and pranks&nbsp;
that the crew has pulled off. With acts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:30.560
of lewd depravity and rampant insanity,&nbsp;
they've elicited both hysterical laughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:34.280
and visceral disgust in equal measure.&nbsp;
We've seen Johnny Knoxville take to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:39.320
sky on a big red rocket and Steve-O perform&nbsp;
the grossest bungee jump anyone has seen.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:43.200
Most of us would flee at the mere thought of&nbsp;
attempting acts like this, but the "Jackass"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:48.000
crew will do it with a smile on their faces. There&nbsp;
have also been pranks of varying scales as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.240
including a limousine packed with a swarm of bees,&nbsp;
as well as a comically giant hand to smack people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:57.320
Needless to say, the creative juices have always&nbsp;
been flowing behind the scenes on "Jackass."

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:01.440
With "Jackass Forever" bringing us things&nbsp;
such as a shock collar game involving a bear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.880
and pogo sticks to the nether regions, where&nbsp;
can they go from here? With people becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.960
increasingly desensitized, the crew will&nbsp;
need to find creative ways to up the ante.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:14.960
With the prospect of a fifth "Jackass" film not&nbsp;
disappearing anytime soon, we need to consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:18.720
who would be returning for another round.&nbsp;
While perhaps in less of a hands-on role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:22.760
Johnny Knoxville would likely return as the&nbsp;
maniacal leader spearheading the whole thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:27.760
Long-serving cast members including Wee Man,&nbsp;
Steve-O, and Chris Pontius have also appeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:32.800
all of the theatrical releases so far, so it is&nbsp;
hoped they would also sign up for more madness.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:37.320
There is also the ever-loyal supporting&nbsp;
cast of Dave England, Preston Lacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:42.000
and Danger Ehren — three men who've never&nbsp;
had issues going above the call of duty.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.560
From being used as human football&nbsp;
goals to playing beehive tetherball,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.534
they've always thrown themselves&nbsp;
headfirst into whatever was needed.

00:09:48.534 --> 00:09:52.440
However, as "Jackass Forever" showed us, the&nbsp;
old guard seems to be passing the torch to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:57.080
new generation of untrained stunt performers.&nbsp;
These fresh faces each have a clear love for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.120
the series, many of them having grown up&nbsp;
with it in the early '00s. It seems that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.400
as long as there are people bold enough&nbsp;
to push themselves to the very limit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.800
then the spirit of "Jackass" will never die.&nbsp;
Whether for a fifth film or for another series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:12.929
it remains to be seen whether we will see&nbsp;
more from our favorite pranksters or not.

